{'symbol': 'LEN', 'date': '2020-06-16 19:30:00', 'title': 'Lennar Reports Second Quarter EPS Of $1.65', 'text': "LENNAR REPORTS SECOND QUARTER EPS OF $1.65.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.65.Q2 REVENUE $5.3 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $5.21 BILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.14 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY DELIVERIES OF 12,672 HOMES, CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR YEAR.NEW ORDERS STALLED SIGNIFICANTLY FROM MID-MARCH TO END OF APRIL, DRIVEN BY COVID-19 & ECONOMIC SHUTDOWN.REVENUES FROM HOME SALES DECREASED 5% IN Q2 TO $4.9 BILLION.QTRLY NEW ORDERS OF 13,015 HOMES,  DOWN 10%.BY QUARTER'S END, TOTAL NEW ORDERS DECLINED BY ONLY 10%, & DELIVERIES ENDED FLAT YEAR-OVER-YEAR.NEW HOME DELIVERIES, EXCLUDING UNCONSOLIDATED ENTITIES, OF 12,653 HOMES IN Q2 WERE FLAT VERSUS 12,706 HOMES IN Q2 OF 2019.BACKLOG OF 17,975 HOMES, DOWN 6% AT QUARTER END.NOW EXPECT 2020 DELIVERIES TO BE IN RANGE OF 50,500 - 51,000 HOMES.AVERAGE SALES PRICE OF HOMES DELIVERED WAS $389,000 IN Q2 VERSUS $407,000 IN Q2 2019.SEES FISCAL YEAR 2020 GROSS MARGIN ON HOME SALES OF ABOUT 21.5% & NET MARGIN ON HOME SALES OF ABOUT 13.0%.LENNAR - GROSS MARGIN ON HOME SALES WAS $1.1 BILLION, OR 21.6%, IN Q2, VERSUS $1.0 BILLION, OR 20.1% IN Q2 OF 2019.QTRLY NEW ORDERS DOLLAR VALUE OF $4.9 BILLION, DOWN 16%.SEES Q3 NEW ORDERS BETWEEN 12,800 - 13,000 HOMES & Q4 NEW ORDERS BETWEEN 12,000 - 12,250 HOMES.SEES Q3 DELIVERIES OF 13,200 - 13,400 HOMES & Q4 DELIVERIES OF 14,300 - 14,600 HOMES.SEES Q3 AVERAGE SALES PRICE BETWEEN $380,000 - $385,000.SEES Q4 AVERAGE SALES PRICE OF $380,000."}
